llama : MoE cache - evict by the pass and by decaying counts, in place of the SLRU

Upstream replaced the cache's LRU with a 50/50 SLRU (#30637). Its victim is
still the least recently used slot, of probation and then of the protected
half, so replayed through bench/moe_cache_sim (EuLLM) it finds the experts the
LRU found, and none when a step wants more experts than there are slots: 0%
of the experts in VRAM for Qwen3-235B with 32 sequences and Qwen3-Coder-480B
with 8, where this eviction keeps 73% and 60%. This patch puts the eviction
below in its place: what were EuLLM's patches 0008 and 0009, one patch since
llama.cpp b11925.

The pass (evict the most recently used slot when a pass wants more experts than the slots):

The cache's slots are shared by all its layers, and the layers come in the same order every step. When a
step selects more experts than there are slots, the least recently used slot always holds an expert of
one of the next layers, the one the step is about to select again, so the least recently used eviction
copies every expert: on LUMI-G (one MI250X GCD, Qwen3-235B Q4_K_M, 3,900 slots of 12,032) 32 sequences
found 0.85% of their experts in VRAM and uploaded 50 GiB a step; Qwen3-Coder-480B found 17% with 8.

The least recently used slot is now evicted only while it is stale: its expert was not selected during the
last pass over the layers. When every slot was used within the last pass, the miss takes the most recently
used slot outside the current layer, whose expert is selected again a whole pass later at the earliest. The
slots filled early in a pass stay and hit in the next one; the rest of the pass goes through the slots last
taken. While a pass's experts fit, a stale slot always exists and the eviction is the plain LRU's, slot for
slot. Replayed through bench/moe_cache_sim (EuLLM) on routing calibrated to the LUMI measurements: the same
hits as LRU with 1 and 8 sequences on the 235B, 72% instead of 0% with 32 (Belady's bound: 81%), 43% to 57%
instead of 0% for the 480B with 8. LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_EVICT=lru evicts the least recently used slot always (as the SLRU does, slot for slot, for these traces).

Statistics: LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_STATS=N counts every step that went through the cache (32 tokens or fewer),
not only those of up to 8, and says which share of the copies went into a slot used within the pass.

LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_TRACE=FILE writes the experts selected in every layer the cache plans (a header, then the
layer, the number of ids and the ids, int32), the input of bench/moe_cache_sim.

The counts (evict by decaying counts among the stale slots and the slots the pass has passed):

The pass rule evicts the least recently used slot while one is stale (its expert unused for a whole pass over the
layers), else the most recently used slot outside the current layer. Replayed on the routing Qwen3-235B and
Qwen3-Coder-480B selected on LUMI-G (one MI250X GCD, LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_TRACE), counts that decay won where the
steps fit and lost where they overflowed the cache, which the pass rule decides by the order of the layers.

Counts are now kept for every expert of every layer, cached or not: each selection adds 1 to a count halved
every 4 passes. A miss takes, among the stale slots, the one whose expert has the lowest count; when every slot
was used within the last pass, the lowest count among the slots used earlier in this pass, whose next use is a
pass away (the most recently used one when there is none yet). The counts are compared as
ln(count) - t*ln(decay), which does not change with time, so a miss compares numbers and computes no decay.

Replayed (bench/moe_cache_sim, lfu-pass), experts found in VRAM, the pass alone -> with the counts: 235B at 8 sequences 88.9% ->
91.0% (copies 98 -> 80 a pass), at 32 56.2% -> 59.9%; 480B at 1 77.2% -> 78.6%, at 8 57.6% -> 61.4%, at 32
16.9% -> 18.9%; the 235B at 1 level (94.3%). The planning costs about 0.4 ms a step more with one sequence and
11 ms with 32 (steps of 47 and 1,540 ms on the GCD). LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_EVICT=pass evicts by the pass
alone, LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_EVICT=lru by the plain LRU.

EuLLM patch on llama.cpp b11925, after 0002.

